---
const stages=[
 {title:'S owns group A',route:'A → S · epoch 1',s:'Open · admitted work may commit',d:'Closed · no copy',copy:'No destination state yet',note:'The durable route names S. All runtime mutations for A must pass S’s transaction-held gate.'},
 {title:'Close admission; drain admitted work',route:'A → S · epoch 1',s:'Closing → closed after drain',d:'Closed',copy:'Wait before copying',note:'Stop new A requests and wait for admitted transactions. Closing the gate waits for their shared gate locks to end. No admitted writer may outlive this boundary.'},
 {title:'Copy the closed group',route:'A → S · epoch 1',s:'Closed · retained source',d:'Closed · receiving A',copy:'Customer → orders → lines/payments → request results',note:'Copy a stable group, including request outcomes. Check exact values, relationships and the complete scope. A copied row does not authorise D to accept a write.'},
 {title:'Validate before changing authority',route:'A → S · epoch 1',s:'Closed',d:'Closed · verified copy',copy:'103: pending · 29.00 · no payment · purchase-103 → 103',note:'The source stays closed while validation completes. If copying fails here, resume or discard the incomplete destination; do not open it.'},
 {title:'Persist the handover decision',route:'A → D · epoch 2',s:'Closed · stale clients rejected',d:'Closed · verified copy',copy:'Route stored durably; destination still closed',note:'Record D as owner before opening it. A crash here leaves a pause. Recovery reads the recorded decision and completes the D handover; it must not reopen S by default.'},
 {title:'Open D; keep S closed',route:'A → D · epoch 2',s:'Closed · refresh route or fail',d:'Open · current owner',copy:'Retry purchase-103 recovers order 103',note:'New requests go to D. The copied outcome resolves purchase-103 without creating another order or decrementing stock again. A stale S connection meets the source gate.'},
 {title:'Later writes belong to D',route:'A → D · epoch 2',s:'Closed · old copy',d:'Open · may now be newer than S',copy:'Returning needs reconciliation or reverse transfer',note:'Once D accepts new writes, S is no longer an immediate return target. A route flip back would lose that work. Keep a tested recovery procedure for the route authority and both databases.'}
];
---
<figure class="pg-figure" data-pg-move aria-labelledby="pg-move-title">
 <figcaption id="pg-move-title"><span class="figure-number">Figure 6</span> A copy becomes the owner</figcaption>
 <p class="pg-stage" data-title data-live>{stages[0].title}</p>
 <div class="entry"><strong>Durable routing authority</strong><span data-route data-live>{stages[0].route}</span></div>
 <div class="move-owners">
  <div data-source class="active"><strong>Source PostgreSQL S</strong><span data-s data-live>{stages[0].s}</span></div>
  <div class="transfer" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
  <div data-destination><strong>Destination PostgreSQL D</strong><span data-d data-live>{stages[0].d}</span></div>
 </div>
 <p class="copy-state" data-copy data-live>{stages[0].copy}</p>
 <p class="pg-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">{stages[0].note}</p>
 <div class="pg-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 6 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 7</span></div>
 <div class="pg-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 <p class="pg-caption">A deliberately paused application handover, with one controller and durable routing authority. Epochs 1/2 are illustrative route generations. They are useful only where enforced. Shared product stock stays outside A; moving A does not transfer stock ownership.</p>
 <details><summary>All handover stages as text</summary><ol>{stages.map(s=><li><strong>{s.title}.</strong> {s.route}. S: {s.s}. D: {s.d}. {s.note}</li>)}</ol></details>
 <script define:vars={{ stages }}>window.__pgMoveStages=stages;</script>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
 const root=document.querySelector('[data-pg-move]');
 if(root){const stages=(window as any).__pgMoveStages;stepper(root,{steps:()=>stages.length,draw:(n)=>{const s=stages[n];['title','route','s','d','copy'].forEach(k=>root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`)!.textContent=s[k]);root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.note;root.querySelector('[data-source]')!.classList.toggle('active',n===0);root.querySelector('[data-destination]')!.classList.toggle('active',n>=5);}});}
</script>
